OL,1,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,2,FTeletextC64D]FHow it works             
OL,3,   EUltimateD]GPetsciiProxy             
OL,4,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,5,BHow it works                           
OL,6, Modern websites hosting teletext       
OL,7, services make use of secure HTTPS      
OL,8, connections. Most C64 networking       
OL,9, devices only support unsecure HTTP.    
OL,11, In order to get teletext on the C64 I  
OL,12, created PetsciiProxy, a 'middle man'   
OL,13, between the C64 and modern internet.   
OL,15,BPetsciiProxy                           
OL,16,FTeletextC64EUltimateGconnects to       
OL,17, petsciiproxy.nl by default. But Petscii
OL,18, Proxy can also be run on your own LAN. 
OL,20, It fetches teletext pages from a       
OL,21, website (mostly HTML) and converts the 
OL,22, data into a binary teletext format.    
OL,23,D]F301G<<                >>F303 B]D1/1  
